WasmFS: backend failures to create a file or directory are reported as EIO

Directory::insertDataFile() and insertDirectory() could only return null,
so open(O_CREAT) and mkdir() turned every backend failure into EIO. They
now return a MaybeFile, which carries a negative error code; the Node
backend reports the host's (EACCES, EROFS, EEXIST, ENOENT, ENAMETOOLONG,
ENOSPC), and inserting into an unlinked directory is ENOENT. Backends that
still return plain null get EIO, as before.

Upstream: not filed yet
Draft: docs/upstream/emscripten-wasmfs-node-create-eio.md

